From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:37:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/18] java: Add the missing JNI binding for
 PDFDocument.setPageTreeCache.

PDFDocument.java declares setPageTreeCache(boolean) and the C function
pdf_set_page_tree_cache() exists, but the JNI implementation was missing,
so calling it threw UnsatisfiedLinkError.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-08.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 platform/java/jni/pdfdocument.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/platform/java/jni/pdfdocument.c b/platform/java/jni/pdfdocument.c
index ce4b2e9..7c4728d 100644
--- a/platform/java/jni/pdfdocument.c
+++ b/platform/java/jni/pdfdocument.c
@@ -385,6 +385,20 @@ FUN(PDFDocument_newDictionary)(JNIEnv *env, jobject self)
 	return jobj;
 }
 
+JNIEXPORT void JNICALL
+FUN(PDFDocument_setPageTreeCache)(JNIEnv *env, jobject self, jboolean enabled)
+{
+	fz_context *ctx = get_context(env);
+	pdf_document *pdf = from_PDFDocument(env, self);
+
+	if (!ctx || !pdf) return;
+
+	fz_try(ctx)
+		pdf_set_page_tree_cache(ctx, pdf, enabled);
+	fz_catch(ctx)
+		jni_rethrow_void(env, ctx);
+}
+
 JNIEXPORT jobject JNICALL
 FUN(PDFDocument_findPage)(JNIEnv *env, jobject self, jint jat)
 {
